  "slug": "rice-adventitious-2660",
  "summary": "Single-cell, spatial and allometric analyses link xylem and root patterning to hydraulics and drought tolerance across wheat, rice and bentgrass.",
  "synthesis": "The items converge on quantitative regulation of organ and vascular anatomy in grasses and its physiological consequences. A xylem single-cell atlas places ZHD3 and ZHD4 at the centre of protoxylem secondary cell wall morphology. In wheat, nodal root anatomy differs by culm position beyond root area scaling, with distinct genetic associations after allometric correction, and metaxylem number is remodelled along root axes, with hydraulic modelling tying vessel patterning to water transport. In rice, OsWOX11 promotes thick AR2 roots, with a higher-activity promoter variant (Hap3), and an RLC3-KNOX module activates lignin genes controlling leaf rolling and drought tolerance. In creeping bentgrass, miR164-NAC dosage separates growth, drought and salt responses via AsNHX1. New here is resolution: cell-type atlases, allometric correction and dosage effects.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
